{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Split landed for review as Gerrit 1934.\n\nCONCERN BOUNDARY: blocking vs never-blocking DET checks — the invariant det_floor.py's own docstring already states. The four never-blocking checks (p2_resolution, p3_package_existence, p6_ac_quality, p7_destructive) plus their private regexes moved to a new sibling det_advisory.py; det_floor.py stays the entry module and re-exports them.\n\nCALL-GRAPH EVIDENCE: the moved set is closed — none of the four calls, or is called by, anything that stayed. P2/P3 reach only grounding.refute_absence; P6 is an aggregation hub over lint detectors already living in siblings; P7 calls nothing. The retained checks are the connected ones (P1+P4 share _count_ac_items, P8 uses est_tokens, P5 uses det_lint's graph helpers). Third application of the seam det_lint (P9) and det_clarity (P10/P11) already used.\n\nSIZES: det_floor.py 793 -> 566 (234 lines / 29% headroom under the 800 cap); det_advisory.py 303. Both inside the 200-500 band.\n\nMODULE-OBJECT BINDINGS (what decided which half moves): DET_CHECKS, run_det_floor and est_tokens are monkeypatched on the det_floor module object by test_plan_review.py, test_af77_config_fault.py and test_plan_review_prerequisites{,_heldout}.py; _clarity_score, _count_ac_items and _description_limit are imported from det_floor by name by the lockstep and migration tests. All six are in the RETAINED half, so those patches still reach live code. No moved symbol is monkeypatched anywhere.\n\nCAUGHT BY THE PLAN REVIEW (G6, first pass BLOCK): p6_ac_quality calls vague_hits_in_line, _lint_verify_command and _verify_command_strings as BARE names bound by det_floor's import block — a body-only move would have raised NameError. det_advisory declares those imports itself; det_floor drops them since P6 was their only consumer. The seam test pins this.\n\nPATH-KEYED REGISTRY SWEEP: .github/complexity-baseline.json has NO entry for det_floor.py, so nothing moved a frozen ceiling and nothing went stale — scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check reads new=0 increased=0 stale=0 (checked directly, not just via make lint), and tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py passes. .github/module-size-limit.txt byte-identical to origin/main. The module-size gate and tests/module_size_support.py enumerate by rglob, so the new file needs no registration. tests/scripts/test_llm_seam_clean_heldout.py _OWNED_FILES/_MARKER_BUDGET needed no change: the module's only config read (_description_limit) stayed, and det_advisory.py carries zero '# read-via:' markers — check_config_ownership.py clean. Prose in registry.py and docs/plan-review-gate.md repointed (comment/doc text only, no assertion touched).\n\nTESTS: RED first — the new seam test failed 18/25 before the split (the 7 passing were premise guards proving the retained half is where the plan claims). GREEN after: 25/25. Zero existing test files modified; the only tests/ addition is the seam test, following the three sibling splits' convention. 1014 passed across every test file that references det_floor. make lint + make typecheck clean."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787188423310772001,"uuid":"cf9e4f1b-9fd5-48be-ae9a-796fdb16f0cd"}